t = t & "(d) ""What are your top priorities right now?"""
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(e) ""How do your goals contribute to your personal growth?"""
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(2) Reality. In this step, supervisors help Sailors explore their current reality and understand where they currently stand in relation to their goal. Sailors mentally assess their strengths, weaknesses, resources, and any obstacles or challenges they may face. It is important for Sailors to have a realistic understanding of their current situation and how it will impact their ability to achieve their goals. Some example questions are:"
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(a) ""What is the current situation or reality regarding this goal?"""
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(b) ""How confident are you in achieving this goal?"""
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(c) ""How much of this goal is under your control?"""
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(d) ""What progress have you made towards your goal so far?"""
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(e) ""What strengths do you have that can help you reach your goal?"""
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(3) Options. Here, supervisors assist Sailors in the exploration of different options and strategies to move closer to their goal; similar to brainstorming. This step encourages creative thinking and generates potential solutions or approaches to overcoming obstacles generated by the Sailors; resulting in instant buy-in as the solutions are self-generated. Some example questions are:"
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(a) ""What are some possible strategies or approaches you could take to achieve your goal?"""
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "[Page 18-7]"
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(b) ""If you had all the resources you needed, what would you do differently?"""
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(c) ""What have you seen others do successfully in similar situations?"""
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(d) ""What are the pros and cons of each option?"""
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(e) ""What options align with your values, strengths, and interests?"""
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & vbCrLf
t = t & "(4) -W-il-l. In the final step, Sailors commits to a specific course of action. They decide on the actions they will take to achieve their goal and create a concrete plan with clear milestones and deadlines. The timeframe for these actions is normally asked for by the supervisor once the Sailors identify their solution. This step also involves exploring the potential support required and developing strategies to stay motivated and overcome challenges. Some example questions are:"
t = t & vbCrLf
